        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-01T09:13:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please don\u0027t use waitForIdle() – instead, use a NetworkCallback and wait for the network to be connected. Return the callback so you can also wait for disconnection in l.421 and the like. The issue is that waitForIdle() is brittle, because it depends on a message having been posted to the handler and on the processing to be finished when the handler becomes idle, both of which are implementation details that can change. Sometimes we don\u0027t have a choice, but here this is a common pattern with a well-defined better option. You can look at `NetworkAgentTest#createConnectedNetworkAgent` for an example.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 382,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 382,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "719b26c45be7ab557f6f5dd9c51d03ad79d28faa",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
