      "message": "Use kotlin.test.assertNotNull instead of junit.frameworks.Assert.assertNotNull. Then you can simplify this by saying\n\n    val networks1 \u003d assertNotNull(service.mIptoNetworksMap...)\n\nThis will immediately fail the test if it\u0027s null and let you remove the question marks below.\n\nAlso suggest inline defining a small helper\n\n    fun getNet(addr: String) \u003d service.mIpToNetworksMap.get(InetAddress.getByName(addr))\n    val networks1 \u003d assertNotNull(getNet(TEST_IPV6_ADDRESS1))\n    val networks2 \u003d assertNotNull(getNet(TEST_IPV4_ADDRESS1))",
